# Copy this file to .env in this same folder (backend\.env), then put your own string below.
#   PowerShell:      Copy-Item backend\.env.example backend\.env
#   macOS / Linux:   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# This is the project's only setting. The ingest window, pipeline.py, every script in database\ and
# the desktop app (frontend\app.py) all read it from backend\.env. (The app can have its own
# frontend\.env instead: see frontend\.env.example. You don't need one.)
#
# DATABASE_URL: your Neon connection string. In the Neon console, open your project, click Connect,
# and copy the string (pooled, with "-pooler" in the host, or direct: both work). Keep
# ?sslmode=require at the end. No quotes and no spaces around "=".
#
# A DATABASE_URL already set in the terminal wins over this file.
# Never commit .env: it holds your database password (.gitignore keeps it out; only this example is shared).

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://neondb_owner:YOUR_PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
